&lt;h1 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Forward Deployed Engineer&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About HSO&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HSO is a global Business Transformation Partner with deep industry expertise and a long standing strategic relationship with Microsoft. We help organisations unlock the full potential of Microsoft Dynamics 365, Azure, Data and AI technologies to modernise operations, accelerate innovation and deliver meaningful business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2026, HSO achieved Microsoft Frontier Partner status, recognising our advanced capabilities across Microsoft Cloud and AI and our ability to help customers move beyond AI experimentation into secure, governed, enterprise scale production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With operations across Europe, North America and Asia, we combine industry knowledge, technical excellence and a practical, people first approach to transformation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we continue to expand our AI capabilities, we’re building a new generation of customer facing engineering talent to help organisations turn the potential of AI and agentic technologies into real, measurable value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HSO is building a new generation of customer facing engineers who will help our customers create the operating model of the future using the latest AI, data and cloud capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forward Deployed Engineers combine consulting judgement, production software engineering, data platform expertise, AI delivery capability and business transformation skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will embed with strategic customers, understand their most important business challenges and rapidly turn those challenges into working, production ready AI applications, agentic workflows, automation solutions and data driven platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands on, outcome led role embedded within customer environments. You’ll move quickly from discovery to working software and take accountability for delivering measurable business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work across business processes, data platforms, integrations, AI, cloud and security, designing solutions that make effective use of Microsoft technologies while integrating with the customer’s wider technology estate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong understanding of modern enterprise data platforms is fundamental to the role. You will need to understand how data is structured, governed, integrated, transformed and made available to AI and application workloads, and how data platform decisions affect the quality, scalability and reliability of the solutions you build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forward Deployed Engineers work closely with Deployment Strategists. The Deployment Strategist focuses on identifying where AI can create the greatest customer value and defining the desired outcome. The FDE takes ownership of how that outcome is delivered technically.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From discovery through to go live, both roles work side by side. The FDE owns the technical solution and delivery, while the Deployment Strategist ensures the solution remains aligned to the business problem and measurable value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role does not end at first deployment. You’ll stay close to solutions through hardening, adoption and handover before moving on to the next value opportunity. You’ll also turn what you learn into reusable HSO assets, reference architectures and delivery patterns that help future engagements move faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Own Customer Outcomes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Embed rapidly within customer teams and develop a strong understanding of their priorities, operating processes, systems, data and constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Translate ambiguous business problems and defined customer outcomes into clear technical delivery plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Act as the technical lead throughout an engagement, guiding customer sponsors, business users, technical teams and HSO colleagues towards successful delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Build trusted relationships with senior operational and technical stakeholders, including CTO and CIO level leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Take ownership for delivering solutions that create measurable customer value rather than simply completing technical tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Lead Discovery and Solution Design&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Lead technical discovery workshops to understand customer challenges and identify high value AI, data and automation opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Assess business processes, data readiness, data architecture, integration points, security requirements, technical risks and operational constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Understand the customer’s existing data platform landscape and identify how data needs to be accessed, transformed, governed or modernised to support the required solution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Apply a problem first approach to identify the smallest valuable solution that can be built and proven quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Design end to end solution architectures that balance speed, scalability, maintainability, security and responsible AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Turn discovery into a pragmatic roadmap from prototype through to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Build and Ship Production Solutions&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Design, build, integrate, test and deploy enterprise grade solutions using modern cloud, data and AI technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Develop AI powered applications, copilots, agents, automations, integrations and workflow solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Build solutions that make effective use of modern enterprise data platforms and ensure AI applications are supported by reliable, governed and accessible data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Integrate solutions with platforms such as Microsoft Fabric, Azure Data Services, Dynamics 365, Power Platform, Salesforce, SAP, ServiceNow and customer owned systems, APIs and data platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Apply modern engineering practices including source control, CI/CD, automated testing, infrastructure as code, observability and secure development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Work iteratively. Deliver value quickly, learn from real world usage and progressively harden solutions for enterprise production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Engineer AI and Agentic Solutions&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Design and implement robust agentic workflows, human in the loop processes and, where appropriate, multi agent architectures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Apply modern techniques across retrieval, grounding, orchestration, tool integration, context engineering and evaluation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Build evaluation frameworks and guardrails to test AI behaviour, reliability and quality before and after deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Implement appropriate responsible AI, security, monitoring and governance controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Ensure data quality, lineage, governance and availability are considered as fundamental components of AI solution design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Use operational data and user feedback to continuously improve solution quality and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Create Reusable HSO Capability&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Reuse existing HSO assets, accelerators and delivery patterns wherever they improve speed and quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Turn lessons from customer engagements into reusable assets, reference architectures, engineering patterns and playbooks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Contribute actively to HSO’s AI, Data, Frontier and Horizon engineering communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Share practical knowledge across regions, practices and delivery teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Support and mentor other engineers as the Forward Deployed Engineering capability grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for experienced engineers who combine strong technical depth with commercial awareness and the ability to operate confidently with customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll ideally bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Significant experience across software engineering, cloud engineering, data engineering, solution development, technical consulting or enterprise technology delivery, with senior level ownership of complex solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong hands on experience building and operating production grade solutions on at least one major cloud platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong understanding and practical experience of modern enterprise data platforms, including data architecture, integration, transformation, governance and the role data plays in enabling AI and application workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience with Microsoft data technologies such as Microsoft Fabric, Azure Data Factory, Azure Synapse, Azure Databricks, OneLake or comparable enterprise data platforms would be highly valuable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Excellent coding capability in a modern language such as Python, C#, TypeScript, JavaScript or Java, with a track record of producing maintainable, production quality software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Practical experience designing, building and deploying AI powered applications using platforms such as Azure AI, OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex AI, Anthropic or comparable technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Hands on experience with large language models, prompting, retrieval augmented generation, evaluation and agent orchestration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong understanding of APIs, integrations, data platforms and modern distributed application architectures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience with modern engineering and DevOps practices including CI/CD, automated testing, source control and infrastructure as code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong customer facing experience in consulting, transformation, delivery or technical leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• The ability to work effectively where requirements are incomplete, priorities evolve quickly and the right answer is not immediately obvious.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• The judgement to balance engineering excellence with speed, practicality and customer value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not need to be an expert in every technology we use. More important is the ability to learn quickly, understand unfamiliar environments and apply strong engineering and data fundamentals to new problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Certifications across Microsoft Azure, Microsoft Fabric, AWS, Google Cloud or leading AI platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience working with enterprise platforms such as Dynamics 365, Power Platform, Salesforce, SAP, ServiceNow or similar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience implementing responsible AI, AI governance, evaluation frameworks or model monitoring in enterprise environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience designing or delivering modern data platforms that support analytics, operational applications or AI workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience across industries such as Manufacturing, Retail, Financial Services, Public Sector or Professional Services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• A track record of turning successful customer solutions into reusable patterns or accelerators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience leading small, highly capable engineering teams from discovery through to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join HSO?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is changing how organisations operate, but most businesses do not need more demonstrations or isolated pilots. They need people who can identify where AI will genuinely create value, ensure the underlying data foundations are fit for purpose and then build something that works in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That is what this role is designed to do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at HSO, you’ll work directly with strategic customers at the point where emerging AI, data and cloud capabilities meet real business problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll have the opportunity to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Build real AI products and solutions rather than proof of concepts that never reach production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Work across AI, cloud and data platforms to solve complex customer problems end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Work directly with senior customer stakeholders and see the impact of what you build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Operate at the forefront of Microsoft’s evolving AI and Data ecosystem as part of a Microsoft Frontier Partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Work across technologies, industries and business problems rather than being confined to a single product or platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Help shape a new engineering capability within HSO rather than stepping into a narrowly defined existing model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Turn successful customer work into reusable technology and approaches that can scale across HSO globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a senior, practical and customer focused team that values ownership, curiosity, engineering quality, speed and measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a competitive base salary alongside HSO’s standard employee benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will also include a performance related element designed to recognise both individual contribution and the value created through successful customer delivery. Further details on the compensation structure and performance measures will be discussed during the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Location: London&lt;br&gt;Type: Full-time&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;BW ESS is seeking an experienced Senior Treasury Manager to take ownership of the Group&#39;s treasury activities across its international corporate entities, project SPVs and joint ventures.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;As BW ESS continues to grow, the complexity and importance of treasury is increasing materially. This role will bring together activities currently undertaken across different parts of the organisation, establish clear ownership and controls, and build a scalable treasury capability for the Group.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This is a senior, hands-on role for someone who can both design the right treasury framework and make sure it operates effectively day to day. We are looking for candidates with real ownership experience in complex, multi-entity, multi-currency environments, ideally gained in energy, renewables, infrastructure, utilities or another project- and SPV-based business.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;About BW ESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;BW ESS is a global energy storage owner-operator, moving with speed to develop, deliver and operate market-leading projects.&amp;nbsp;The business is active in the UK, Australia, Italy, Germany, Spain, and Sweden. It has more than 540MWh of operating Battery Energy Storage Systems (BESS), with ~12GWh under construction and a development pipeline of several gigawatts.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Part of BW Group, BW ESS builds on decades of global infrastructure experience, takes a long-term view of projects and partnerships, and focuses on unlocking value throughout the energy storage asset lifecycle.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;To find out more, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://bw-ess.com/&quot;&gt;https://bw-ess.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Reporting to the Director of FP&amp;amp;A and Treasury, you will work closely with the CFO, Strategic Finance, Portfolio FP&amp;amp;A, Accounting, Tax, Investments, Legal and project teams, as well as BW Group and the Group&#39;s banking counterparties.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;You will be responsible for Group cash and liquidity management, credit support, FX and hedging operations, cash investment, banking and treasury facilities, treasury governance and treasury systems.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Your objective is to replace fragmented activity with a coherent Group treasury capability: giving management reliable visibility of cash, liquidity and treasury risk, ensuring cash and credit resources are deployed efficiently, strengthening controls and banking infrastructure, and building processes and systems that scale with the business.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cash management: own the consolidated Group cash position across corporate entities, project SPVs, joint ventures, accounts and currencies, including restricted and unrestricted cash, intercompany funding, equity contributions and distributions, and ensuring the right cash sits in the right entity, account and currency ahead of material payment obligations.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Liquidity management: own the Group liquidity position and rolling forecast, consolidating inputs from Portfolio FP&amp;amp;A, Accounting, Investments, Strategic Finance and project teams, and providing forward-looking analysis of requirements, constraints, surpluses and funding needs across multiple currencies and jurisdictions.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Credit support: own the portfolio of bank guarantees, parent-company guarantees, letters of credit and other contingent exposures, managing issuance, amendment, renewal and cancellation, and monitoring utilisation, expiries, fees, collateral and facility headroom.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;FX management: own the consolidated view of forecast and actual FX exposures across development, construction, operations and corporate activity, maintain the Group&#39;s FX framework, recommend hedging actions, and execute approved transactions within delegated authorities.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cash investment: manage surplus cash within approved policies and counterparty limits, optimising deposit arrangements, managing counterparty exposure and diversification, and negotiating terms to improve returns while preserving liquidity.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Hedging operations: own the operational management of FX and interest-rate derivatives, including execution, confirmation, settlement, records of hedges and maturities, collateral and threshold monitoring, and treasury inputs into valuation, accounting and reporting.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Banking and facilities: act as principal treasury relationship owner for cash-management and transaction banks, maintain the Group&#39;s banking architecture (accounts, mandates, signatories, access, KYC and documentation), own treasury-related facilities, and support complex funds flows for acquisitions, disposals, financings, refinancings and project financial close.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Controls, policy and governance: own treasury policies, procedures, delegated authorities and the control framework, ensure transactions are authorised, documented, reconciled and auditable, monitor compliance with policy and counterparty limits, and report to senior management and governance forums.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Systems and transformation: define the future treasury operating model, lead Treasury&#39;s contribution to the Group&#39;s ERP implementation, drive automation of cash visibility, forecasting, payments and bank-statement collection, and assess the role and timing of a dedicated Treasury Management System.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;10+ years&#39; relevant experience in corporate treasury, infrastructure, energy, banking or a closely related finance role.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Demonstrable experience taking ownership of treasury activities in a complex, multi-entity, multi-currency organisation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Strong practical experience across cash and liquidity management, FX, banking, credit support and treasury controls.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience managing senior relationships with banks and other financial counterparties.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Strong understanding of treasury risk management, with the ability to translate financial exposures into practical recommendations and actions.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Ability to operate effectively across multiple legal entities, jurisdictions, currencies and stakeholders.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Strong judgement and the confidence to identify issues, challenge existing practice and recommend solutions to senior management.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Comfortable working hands-on while building more scalable processes, controls and systems.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Strong analytical capability and the ability to communicate complex treasury issues clearly and concisely.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;ACT, ACA, ACCA, CIMA or equivalent professional qualification preferred.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Energy, renewables, infrastructure, utilities or another project- and SPV-based business.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Treasury within a business undergoing rapid international growth.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Project finance, including restricted cash, reserve accounts and project-level funding structures.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Bank guarantees, letters of credit, parent-company guarantees and other project credit support.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;FX and interest-rate derivatives, including ISDA-governed arrangements.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;ERP, Treasury Management System or wider finance-transformation implementation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cash pooling, bank connectivity, automated payments and treasury reporting.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Acquisition, disposal, refinancing and complex transaction funds flows.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join BW ESS?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This is an opportunity to join a fast-moving global energy storage owner-operator at a pivotal point in its growth, and to build the Group&#39;s treasury capability from a position of genuine ownership.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;If you are an experienced treasury professional who enjoys combining framework-building with hands-on delivery in an international, project-based business, we would like to hear from you.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;BW ESS is committed to building a high-performing, inclusive team and welcomes applications from candidates of all backgrounds&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Your personal information will be processed in accordance with our &lt;a href=&quot;https://bw-ess.com/bw-ess-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Join us in shaping the experience that millions of customers land on every time they open DoorDash, Wolt, or Deliveroo. As part of our Core Consumer organisation, our Homepage team owns one of the single biggest levers we have on what customers find and one of the hardest surfaces in the app to get right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at the intersection of ranking, personalisation, and AI/ML, you&#39;ll help decide what each customer sees and why, across three brands and dozens of markets. You&#39;ll be building on a global stack, and your roadmap will be a mix: global platform problems that apply worldwide, global capabilities we&#39;re accelerating into EMEA, and EMEA-specific problems worth solving properly rather than working around.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Product Manager to join our Homepage team. In this role, you&#39;ll shape how customers discover restaurants, grocery and retail venues, dishes and products — and help define what discovery looks like as AI-driven and agentic experiences change the way people decide what to order.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining a team working on one of the most-used surfaces in the app.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&#39;s what your day-to-day might look like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building new end-to-end features and user experiences on Homepage that shape how customers discover restaurants, grocery and retail venues, dishes, and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on ranking, personalisation, and AI/ML problems in the Homepage domain, including how we decide what each customer sees and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exploring where AI-driven and agentic experiences change the way customers discover what to order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making discovery work across three brands and many markets, without flattening into one-size-fits-all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need to Thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ideal candidate will bring strong product judgment and curiosity to grow into the rest:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Product Manager on consumer-facing products - discovery, homepage, feed, or ranking-driven experiences are especially relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a product manager more than a feature owner. Someone who finds the customer problems that matter most and makes the case for solving them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work backwards from the customer problem, and weigh it against what the business needs most right now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable holding several business objectives at once and making a call when they pull in different directions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well with a wide range of stakeholders and build trust with people whose priorities differ from your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think strategically and can move between long-term direction and what we should ship next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable with ambiguity and genuinely flexible (this industry is changing fast, AI most of all).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re curious about what AI actually changes for customers, and can tell real value from hype.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Next steps&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position will be filled as soon as we find the right person, so make sure to apply as soon as you realize you really, really want to join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ncz4s_oBczc?si=FzuwoSOLcv5WZVRN&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
